From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pam_inline: fix memset_explicit call for glibc 2.43

glibc 2.43 exposes memset_explicit() with the standard three-argument
signature:

  memset_explicit(void *dest, int ch, size_t len)

Linux-PAM 1.5.3 incorrectly calls it with only two arguments in
pam_overwrite_n(), which causes compilation failures once the newer glibc
headers are in the target sysroot.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [compatibility fix for newer glibc headers]
Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 libpam/include/pam_inline.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libpam/include/pam_inline.h b/libpam/include/pam_inline.h
index 3f26b16..9b97327 100644
--- a/libpam/include/pam_inline.h
+++ b/libpam/include/pam_inline.h
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ pam_str_skip_icase_prefix_len(const char *str, const char *prefix, size_t prefix
 static inline void pam_overwrite_n(void *ptr, size_t len)
 {
 	if (ptr)
-		memset_explicit(ptr, len);
+		memset_explicit(ptr, 0, len);
 }
 #elif defined HAVE_EXPLICIT_BZERO
 static inline void pam_overwrite_n(void *ptr, size_t len)
-- 
2.43.0
